{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_09-22-17-omnipaxos-real-run/agent-source/omnipaxos/src && sed -n '385,412p' storage/internal_storage.rs && echo \\\"=== 469-474 ===\\\" && sed -n '469,474p' storage/internal_storage.rs\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_09-22-17-omnipaxos-real-run/agent-source/omnipaxos/src && sed -n '385,412p' storage/internal_storage.rs && echo \\\"=== 469-474 ===\\\" && sed -n '469,474p' storage/internal_storage.rs\"","aggregated_output":"    // Creates a Delta snapshot of entries from `from_idx` to the end of the decided log and also\n    // returns the compacted idx of the created snapshot. If the range of entries contains entries\n    // which have already been compacted a valid delta cannot be created, so creates a Complete\n    // snapshot of the entire decided log instead.\n    pub(crate) fn create_diff_snapshot(\n        &self,\n        from_idx: usize,\n    ) -> StorageResult<(Option<SnapshotType<T>>, usize)> {\n        let log_decided_idx = self.get_decided_idx_without_stopsign();\n        let compacted_idx = self.get_compacted_idx();\n        let snapshot = if from_idx <= compacted_idx {\n            // Some entries in range are compacted, snapshot entire decided log\n            if compacted_idx < log_decided_idx {\n                Some(SnapshotType::Complete(\n                    self.create_snapshot(log_decided_idx)?,\n                ))\n            } else {\n                // Entire decided log already snapshotted\n                self.get_snapshot()?.map(|s| SnapshotType::Complete(s))\n            }\n        } else {\n            let diff_entries = self.get_entries(from_idx, log_decided_idx)?;\n            Some(SnapshotType::Delta(T::Snapshot::create(\n                diff_entries.as_slice(),\n            )))\n        };\n        Ok((snapshot, log_decided_idx))\n    }\n=== 469-474 ===\n    fn get_decided_idx_without_stopsign(&self) -> usize {\n        match self.stopsign_is_decided() {\n            true => self.get_decided_idx() - 1,\n            false => self.get_decided_idx(),\n        }\n    }\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_09-22-17-omnipaxos-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nR1=\\\"8b314551f1e049fcbf73a358f8ddf2c8\\\"\nR2=\\\"9125b6a531234e7d9d2fa8cbb817df63\\\"\nQC=\\\"27bf7fc0875c4342966bd3dc15df80ec-question-0\\\"\nK1=\\\"27bf7fc0875c4342966bd3dc15df80ec-knowledge-0\\\"\nK2=\\\"3ed5ddd94bce4e94a2dc5b7bb417c18a-knowledge-1\\\"\n\nsources=[\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"create_diff_snapshot\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"omnipaxos/src/storage/internal_storage.rs\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":385,\\\"end_line\\\":412,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"no_stopsign_decided_idx\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"omnipaxos/src/storage/internal_storage.rs\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":469,\\\"end_line\\\":474,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}\n]\nk2={\n \\\"id\\\":K2,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":\\\"On a replica that already holds the accepted StopSign, applying an AcceptSync whose LogSync carries that StopSign leaves the stored log unchanged while the reported accepted index rises by one; the replica's read of the StopSign's previous index (5) then returns None, its read of index 6 returns the StopSign, and read_decided_suffix(0) returns a decided log that omits the five entries: one element (the StopSign) when the replica's decided index has been pushed past the StopSign's index, and an empty list when its decided index still stops at that index.\\\",\n \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Three-node cluster, five decided entries plus a StopSign, no snapshots (NoSnapshot), default batch size, re-synchronization triggered by a follower's public reconnected() call after the StopSign was accepted and decided. Both variants were observed: two followers re-synchronize (receipt 8b314551f1e049fcbf73a358f8ddf2c8 events 22, 23 with a one-element decided read; receipt 9125b6a531234e7d9d2fa8cbb817df63 events 22, 23) and only one follower re-synchronizes (receipt 9125b6a531234e7d9d2fa8cbb817df63 event 35 with an empty decided read and decided index 6), always against the same replica's pre-resynchronization state (6/6, six-element read) and the no-reconnect control.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"sync_log_accounting\\\",\\\"create_log_sync\\\",\\\"internal_get_entry_type\\\",\\\"internal_read_range\\\",\\\"create_read_log_entries\\\",\\\"read_decided_suffix_public\\\",\\\"memory_storage_read_helpers\\\"],\n \\\"executions\\\":{R1:[19,20,22,23],R2:[21,22,23,34,35]},\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\\\"entry_id\\\":K1,\\\"revision\\\":2,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"sync_log adds the StopSign carried by LogSync on top of sync_idx + suffix.len()\\\"}],\n \\\"changed_premise\\\":\\\"Generalizes the decided-log read effect from one observed decided-index position to both observed positions: with a quorum of inflated reports the leader's phantom decision pushes the replica's decided index past the StopSign index and the read keeps the StopSign alone, while with a single inflated report the decided index stays at the StopSign index and the read returns an empty list.\\\",\n \\\"affected_uses\\\":[\\\"3ed5ddd94bce4e94a2dc5b7bb417c18a-interpretation-0\\\"]\n}\nk3={\n \\\"ref\\\":\\\"@inflation_applicability\\\",\n \\\"kind\\\":\\\"fact\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":\\\"The inflated accepted index follows from the resume point being compared against the index the StopSign occupies in the receiving replica's accounting: sync_log computes accepted_idx = LogSync.sync_idx + LogSync.suffix.len() and adds one for a carried StopSign, while the StopSign occupies the index accepted_idx - 1 and the sender attaches it without shifting sync_idx. The condition is therefore sync_idx + suffix.len() >= the StopSign's index, and it does not depend on the snapshot option: the no-snapshot branch passes the caller's common_prefix_idx unchanged (the follower's accepted index, which already counts the StopSign), whereas the snapshot branch passes the compacted index returned by create_diff_snapshot, which is derived from get_decided_idx_without_stopsign and therefore excludes the StopSign.\\\",\n \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Holds for any LogSync whose stopsign is Some; the snapshot branch is only entered when T::Snapshot::use_snapshots() is true and the sender's decided index exceeds common_prefix_idx. Sourced from the captured snapshot; the observed inflation (receipts 8b314551f1e049fcbf73a358f8ddf2c8 and 9125b6a531234e7d9d2fa8cbb817df63) is a no-snapshot instance of the condition and no snapshot-enabled execution has been run.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"sync_log_accounting\\\",\\\"create_log_sync\\\",\\\"create_diff_snapshot\\\",\\\"no_stopsign_decided_idx\\\",\\\"send_accsync_valid_entries\\\"],\n \\\"executions\\\":{R2:[19,22,23,35]}\n}\nk4={\n \\\"ref\\\":\\\"@leader_decides_without_log_bound\\\",\n \\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":\\\"A leader in the accept phase accepts a decision at the accepted index reported by any matching-ballot Accepted message: it records that index for the sender, and if the index exceeds its own decided index and a write quorum of recorded accepted indexes covers it, it sets its decided index to exactly that reported index, without comparing it against the length of its own log or against its own accepted index.\\\",\n \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Leader role in Phase::Accept with a matching ballot; the recorded accepted indexes include the leader's own slot as it was last written by its own accept handling. Observed: with two inflated reports the leader reported decided index 7 while holding six indices and its own accepted index stayed 6 (receipt 8b314551f1e049fcbf73a358f8ddf2c8 event 24; reproduced in receipt 9125b6a531234e7d9d2fa8cbb817df63 event 24), while with a single inflated report no write quorum was reached and the leader stayed at 6/6 (receipt 9125b6a531234e7d9d2fa8cbb817df63 event 37).\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"leader_decision_on_accepted\\\",\\\"accepted_idx_public_doc\\\",\\\"is_reconfigured_endpoint\\\"],\n \\\"executions\\\":{R1:[24],R2:[24,37]}\n}\n\nrationale=(\n \\\"The isolating successor run confirms and narrows the account. Receipt 9125b6a531234e7d9d2fa8cbb817df63 (same harness lineage, third case added; all three tests passed) showed: with only node 1 re-synchronized, node 1 alone ended at accepted 7 over the same six indices of content, decided 6, so its own reported reconfiguration endpoint flipped from true to false, its read of the StopSign's index 5 returned None while its read of index 6 returned the StopSign, and its decided-log read from 0 returned an empty list where it had returned six elements before (event 35); nodes 2 and 3 stayed at 6/6 with a six-element decided read and is_reconfigured true (events 36, 37). That separates the two consequences: the follower-local inflation and endpoint/read corruption need only one re-synchronized replica, while the leader's decision at index 7 requires a write quorum of inflated reports (the two-follower case, event 24 in both receipts). The comparisons match: on the single case, comparisons 3-6 (node 1 reports the reconfiguration as decided; its decided index is covered by the entries it holds; its StopSign stays at index 5; its decided log keeps six elements) were violated at index 35, while comparisons 7-8 (the leader still reports the reconfiguration as decided and stays consistent) hold at index 37; comparison 2 holds the baseline that index 6 held no StopSign before the re-synchronization (index 19). The declared defect stands: a public reconnected() call on a replica that has accepted the configuration's StopSign corrupts that replica's index accounting, hides the configuration transition from the user, and - with a write quorum of such reports - makes the leader declare a decided index past every entry it holds, after which the leader itself no longer reports the reconfiguration as decided and cannot read its decided log at all.\\\"\n)\ncounterevidence=[\n \\\"The no-reconnect control of the same execution kept every endpoint consistent (accepted 6, decided 6, is_reconfigured true, six-element decided read; receipt 8b314551f1e049fcbf73a358f8ddf2c8 events 9-11 and the control case of the successor run), so the deviation is caused by the re-established-connection path rather than by the reconfiguration, the harness or the reading.\\\",\n \\\"The single-replica case limits the leader-side consequence: one inflated report did not reach a write quorum, so the leader kept decided 6 with is_reconfigured true (receipt 9125b6a531234e7d9d2fa8cbb817df63 event 37); the decision at the phantom index therefore requires a write quorum of inflated reports (both followers of a three-node cluster) within one term.\\\",\n \\\"The documented reconfiguration flow (agent-source/docs/omnipaxos/reconfiguration.md 25-34) expects the user to start a new instance once a node observes LogEntry::StopSign(ss, true), so a user who stops the old instance immediately narrows the user-facing window; the defect still bites the leader, which never observes the decision after the corruption, and any replica whose log is read while its old instance still runs.\\\",\n \\\"The leader's phantom decision is inferred from its reported state (decided 7 with accepted 6 and six indices of content) plus the followers' inflated 7; the internal accepted-index vector was not sampled, so which reports formed the quorum rests on the source rule that any matching-ballot Accepted index counts, not on a direct trace.\\\"\n]\nlimitations=[\n \\\"No snapshot-enabled execution has been run; the sourced applicability fact says the snapshot branch computes sync_idx without the StopSign, so the defect is not specific to NoSnapshot entries, but that branch was not exercised.\\\",\n \\\"Messages were delivered in FIFO order without loss and without tick()-driven timers, so the re-established-connection call is the only recovery trigger exercised; a loss-triggered re-synchronization path that produces the same resume point is untested.\\\",\n \\\"The consequence is bounded by the sealed configuration: after the StopSign is accepted no further entries can be accepted, so the phantom decided index carries no value and no value can be mis-assigned; the demonstrated effects are the corrupted index accounting, the unreadable or blank decided log, and the lost reconfiguration endpoint rather than divergent values.\\\",\n \\\"All three nodes used in-memory storage; persistence across a restart and other storages' behaviour on out-of-range reads (a storage-implementer responsibility per the Storage trait) were not exercised.\\\",\n \\\"Only three-node clusters with a single uninterrupted term were exercised; larger clusters and repeated leader changes around the re-synchronization were not.\\\"\n]\ninterp={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":QC,\n \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"3ed5ddd94bce4e94a2dc5b7bb417c18a-experiment\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"sync_log_accounting\\\",\\\"create_log_sync\\\",\\\"send_accsync_valid_entries\\\",\\\"handle_promise_accept_resync\\\",\\\"leader_decision_on_accepted\\\",\\\"stopsign_is_decided_predicate\\\",\\\"is_reconfigured_endpoint\\\",\\\"logentry_stopsign_contract\\\",\\\"reconfig_user_flow\\\",\\\"accepted_idx_public_doc\\\",\\\"internal_read_range\\\",\\\"internal_get_entry_type\\\",\\\"create_read_log_entries\\\",\\\"memory_storage_read_helpers\\\",\\\"create_diff_snapshot\\\",\\\"no_stopsign_decided_idx\\\"],\n \\\"executions\\\":{R1:[19,20,21,22,23,24,9,10,11],R2:[19,22,23,24,35,36,37]},\n \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\n \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":rationale,\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":counterevidence,\n \\\"limitations\\\":limitations,\n \\\"joint_history\\\":\\\"Two successive invocations of the same harness lineage, read separately and not combined: receipt 8b314551f1e049fcbf73a358f8ddf2c8 ran the fixed experiment 27bf7fc0875c4342966bd3dc15df80ec-experiment (resync and control cases) and receipt 9125b6a531234e7d9d2fa8cbb817df63 ran its declared successor 3ed5ddd94bce4e94a2dc5b7bb417c18a-experiment (same prefix and cases plus a single-follower case and a read of index 6). Both were produced from the same three-node setup (MemoryStorage, NoSnapshot entries, batch size 1, FIFO delivery without loss) with the same public endpoints; the successor reproduces the resync witness (events 22, 23, 24) and adds the isolated single-replica witness (event 35) and the leader-side hold (event 37). Event index 19 in both receipts is the same pre-resynchronization sampling point.\\\",\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\\\"entry_id\\\":K1,\\\"revision\\\":2,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"sync_log double-counts the StopSign when the resumed prefix already contains it\\\"},{\\\"entry_id\\\":K2,\\\"revision\\\":2,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"a re-synchronized replica's decided log read loses the entries\\\"},{\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"@inflation_applicability\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"the condition is the resume point covering the StopSign's index\\\"},{\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"@leader_decides_without_log_bound\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"the leader decides the reported accepted index without bounding it to its own log\\\"}]\n}\ngap={\\\"investigation_id\\\":QC,\n \\\"question\\\":\\\"Does the same inflation occur when T::Snapshot::use_snapshots() is true (the snapshot branch is not entered in the observed scenario because the sender's decided index equals the resume point), and can a leader's own accepted index be inflated when handle_majority_promises applies a follower's LogSync whose stopsign is Some and whose sync_idx already covers the StopSign?\\\"}\nquestion={\\\"id\\\":QC,\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"active\\\",\n \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"Whether a snapshot-enabled configuration reproduces the inflation or the sourced branch difference prevents it, and whether a new leader that already decided the StopSign is inflated when it syncs from a follower at a higher accepted round (the candidate's own decided index becomes sync_idx).\\\"}\n\nupdate={\\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Interpret the successor receipt, correct the knowledge it changes and register the remaining applicability question. The isolating run confirmed the follower-local consequence with a single re-synchronized replica (its endpoint flips and its decided-log read loses all six elements, receipt 9125b6a531234e7d9d2fa8cbb817df63 event 35) while the leader stayed consistent (event 37), which shows the leader's decision at the phantom index 7 requires a write quorum of inflated reports, as reproduced in events 22-24 of the same receipt and in the earlier receipt. The interpretation now covers both receipts with the same-run controls, a limitation narrows the consequence to index accounting and readability because the sealed configuration admits no further entries, the index-shift behavior is generalized to both observed decided-index positions, two behaviors/facts are added (the decision rule that ignores the leader's own log bound, and the sourced applicability condition including its independence from the snapshot option), and one gap is registered for the snapshot branch and for a new leader applying a follower's LogSync.\\\"),\n \\\"sources\\\":sources,\n \\\"investigations\\\":[question],\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[k2,k3,k4],\n \\\"gaps\\\":[gap],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[interp]}\njson.dump(update, open('update.json','w'), indent=1)\nprint('written')\nPY\ntimeout 120 /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_09-22-17-omnipaxos-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -c 2000\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_09-22-17-omnipaxos-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nR1=\\\"8b314551f1e049fcbf73a358f8ddf2c8\\\"\nR2=\\\"9125b6a531234e7d9d2fa8cbb817df63\\\"\nQC=\\\"27bf7fc0875c4342966bd3dc15df80ec-question-0\\\"\nK1=\\\"27bf7fc0875c4342966bd3dc15df80ec-knowledge-0\\\"\nK2=\\\"3ed5ddd94bce4e94a2dc5b7bb417c18a-knowledge-1\\\"\n\nsources=[\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"create_diff_snapshot\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"omnipaxos/src/storage/internal_storage.rs\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":385,\\\"end_line\\\":412,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"no_stopsign_decided_idx\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"omnipaxos/src/storage/internal_storage.rs\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":469,\\\"end_line\\\":474,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}\n]\nk2={\n \\\"id\\\":K2,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":\\\"On a replica that already holds the accepted StopSign, applying an AcceptSync whose LogSync carries that StopSign leaves the stored log unchanged while the reported accepted index rises by one; the replica's read of the StopSign's previous index (5) then returns None, its read of index 6 returns the StopSign, and read_decided_suffix(0) returns a decided log that omits the five entries: one element (the StopSign) when the replica's decided index has been pushed past the StopSign's index, and an empty list when its decided index still stops at that index.\\\",\n \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Three-node cluster, five decided entries plus a StopSign, no snapshots (NoSnapshot), default batch size, re-synchronization triggered by a follower's public reconnected() call after the StopSign was accepted and decided. Both variants were observed: two followers re-synchronize (receipt 8b314551f1e049fcbf73a358f8ddf2c8 events 22, 23 with a one-element decided read; receipt 9125b6a531234e7d9d2fa8cbb817df63 events 22, 23) and only one follower re-synchronizes (receipt 9125b6a531234e7d9d2fa8cbb817df63 event 35 with an empty decided read and decided index 6), always against the same replica's pre-resynchronization state (6/6, six-element read) and the no-reconnect control.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"sync_log_accounting\\\",\\\"create_log_sync\\\",\\\"internal_get_entry_type\\\",\\\"internal_read_range\\\",\\\"create_read_log_entries\\\",\\\"read_decided_suffix_public\\\",\\\"memory_storage_read_helpers\\\"],\n \\\"executions\\\":{R1:[19,20,22,23],R2:[21,22,23,34,35]},\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\\\"entry_id\\\":K1,\\\"revision\\\":2,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"sync_log adds the StopSign carried by LogSync on top of sync_idx + suffix.len()\\\"}],\n \\\"changed_premise\\\":\\\"Generalizes the decided-log read effect from one observed decided-index position to both observed positions: with a quorum of inflated reports the leader's phantom decision pushes the replica's decided index past the StopSign index and the read keeps the StopSign alone, while with a single inflated report the decided index stays at the StopSign index and the read returns an empty list.\\\",\n \\\"affected_uses\\\":[\\\"3ed5ddd94bce4e94a2dc5b7bb417c18a-interpretation-0\\\"]\n}\nk3={\n \\\"ref\\\":\\\"@inflation_applicability\\\",\n \\\"kind\\\":\\\"fact\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":\\\"The inflated accepted index follows from the resume point being compared against the index the StopSign occupies in the receiving replica's accounting: sync_log computes accepted_idx = LogSync.sync_idx + LogSync.suffix.len() and adds one for a carried StopSign, while the StopSign occupies the index accepted_idx - 1 and the sender attaches it without shifting sync_idx. The condition is therefore sync_idx + suffix.len() >= the StopSign's index, and it does not depend on the snapshot option: the no-snapshot branch passes the caller's common_prefix_idx unchanged (the follower's accepted index, which already counts the StopSign), whereas the snapshot branch passes the compacted index returned by create_diff_snapshot, which is derived from get_decided_idx_without_stopsign and therefore excludes the StopSign.\\\",\n \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Holds for any LogSync whose stopsign is Some; the snapshot branch is only entered when T::Snapshot::use_snapshots() is true and the sender's decided index exceeds common_prefix_idx. Sourced from the captured snapshot; the observed inflation (receipts 8b314551f1e049fcbf73a358f8ddf2c8 and 9125b6a531234e7d9d2fa8cbb817df63) is a no-snapshot instance of the condition and no snapshot-enabled execution has been run.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"sync_log_accounting\\\",\\\"create_log_sync\\\",\\\"create_diff_snapshot\\\",\\\"no_stopsign_decided_idx\\\",\\\"send_accsync_valid_entries\\\"],\n \\\"executions\\\":{R2:[19,22,23,35]}\n}\nk4={\n \\\"ref\\\":\\\"@leader_decides_without_log_bound\\\",\n \\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":\\\"A leader in the accept phase accepts a decision at the accepted index reported by any matching-ballot Accepted message: it records that index for the sender, and if the index exceeds its own decided index and a write quorum of recorded accepted indexes covers it, it sets its decided index to exactly that reported index, without comparing it against the length of its own log or against its own accepted index.\\\",\n \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Leader role in Phase::Accept with a matching ballot; the recorded accepted indexes include the leader's own slot as it was last written by its own accept handling. Observed: with two inflated reports the leader reported decided index 7 while holding six indices and its own accepted index stayed 6 (receipt 8b314551f1e049fcbf73a358f8ddf2c8 event 24; reproduced in receipt 9125b6a531234e7d9d2fa8cbb817df63 event 24), while with a single inflated report no write quorum was reached and the leader stayed at 6/6 (receipt 9125b6a531234e7d9d2fa8cbb817df63 event 37).\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"leader_decision_on_accepted\\\",\\\"accepted_idx_public_doc\\\",\\\"is_reconfigured_endpoint\\\"],\n \\\"executions\\\":{R1:[24],R2:[24,37]}\n}\n\nrationale=(\n \\\"The isolating successor run confirms and narrows the account. Receipt 9125b6a531234e7d9d2fa8cbb817df63 (same harness lineage, third case added; all three tests passed) showed: with only node 1 re-synchronized, node 1 alone ended at accepted 7 over the same six indices of content, decided 6, so its own reported reconfiguration endpoint flipped from true to false, its read of the StopSign's index 5 returned None while its read of index 6 returned the StopSign, and its decided-log read from 0 returned an empty list where it had returned six elements before (event 35); nodes 2 and 3 stayed at 6/6 with a six-element decided read and is_reconfigured true (events 36, 37). That separates the two consequences: the follower-local inflation and endpoint/read corruption need only one re-synchronized replica, while the leader's decision at index 7 requires a write quorum of inflated reports (the two-follower case, event 24 in both receipts). The comparisons match: on the single case, comparisons 3-6 (node 1 reports the reconfiguration as decided; its decided index is covered by the entries it holds; its StopSign stays at index 5; its decided log keeps six elements) were violated at index 35, while comparisons 7-8 (the leader still reports the reconfiguration as decided and stays consistent) hold at index 37; comparison 2 holds the baseline that index 6 held no StopSign before the re-synchronization (index 19). The declared defect stands: a public reconnected() call on a replica that has accepted the configuration's StopSign corrupts that replica's index accounting, hides the configuration transition from the user, and - with a write quorum of such reports - makes the leader declare a decided index past every entry it holds, after which the leader itself no longer reports the reconfiguration as decided and cannot read its decided log at all.\\\"\n)\ncounterevidence=[\n \\\"The no-reconnect control of the same execution kept every endpoint consistent (accepted 6, decided 6, is_reconfigured true, six-element decided read; receipt 8b314551f1e049fcbf73a358f8ddf2c8 events 9-11 and the control case of the successor run), so the deviation is caused by the re-established-connection path rather than by the reconfiguration, the harness or the reading.\\\",\n \\\"The single-replica case limits the leader-side consequence: one inflated report did not reach a write quorum, so the leader kept decided 6 with is_reconfigured true (receipt 9125b6a531234e7d9d2fa8cbb817df63 event 37); the decision at the phantom index therefore requires a write quorum of inflated reports (both followers of a three-node cluster) within one term.\\\",\n \\\"The documented reconfiguration flow (agent-source/docs/omnipaxos/reconfiguration.md 25-34) expects the user to start a new instance once a node observes LogEntry::StopSign(ss, true), so a user who stops the old instance immediately narrows the user-facing window; the defect still bites the leader, which never observes the decision after the corruption, and any replica whose log is read while its old instance still runs.\\\",\n \\\"The leader's phantom decision is inferred from its reported state (decided 7 with accepted 6 and six indices of content) plus the followers' inflated 7; the internal accepted-index vector was not sampled, so which reports formed the quorum rests on the source rule that any matching-ballot Accepted index counts, not on a direct trace.\\\"\n]\nlimitations=[\n \\\"No snapshot-enabled execution has been run; the sourced applicability fact says the snapshot branch computes sync_idx without the StopSign, so the defect is not specific to NoSnapshot entries, but that branch was not exercised.\\\",\n \\\"Messages were delivered in FIFO order without loss and without tick()-driven timers, so the re-established-connection call is the only recovery trigger exercised; a loss-triggered re-synchronization path that produces the same resume point is untested.\\\",\n \\\"The consequence is bounded by the sealed configuration: after the StopSign is accepted no further entries can be accepted, so the phantom decided index carries no value and no value can be mis-assigned; the demonstrated effects are the corrupted index accounting, the unreadable or blank decided log, and the lost reconfiguration endpoint rather than divergent values.\\\",\n \\\"All three nodes used in-memory storage; persistence across a restart and other storages' behaviour on out-of-range reads (a storage-implementer responsibility per the Storage trait) were not exercised.\\\",\n \\\"Only three-node clusters with a single uninterrupted term were exercised; larger clusters and repeated leader changes around the re-synchronization were not.\\\"\n]\ninterp={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":QC,\n \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"3ed5ddd94bce4e94a2dc5b7bb417c18a-experiment\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"sync_log_accounting\\\",\\\"create_log_sync\\\",\\\"send_accsync_valid_entries\\\",\\\"handle_promise_accept_resync\\\",\\\"leader_decision_on_accepted\\\",\\\"stopsign_is_decided_predicate\\\",\\\"is_reconfigured_endpoint\\\",\\\"logentry_stopsign_contract\\\",\\\"reconfig_user_flow\\\",\\\"accepted_idx_public_doc\\\",\\\"internal_read_range\\\",\\\"internal_get_entry_type\\\",\\\"create_read_log_entries\\\",\\\"memory_storage_read_helpers\\\",\\\"create_diff_snapshot\\\",\\\"no_stopsign_decided_idx\\\"],\n \\\"executions\\\":{R1:[19,20,21,22,23,24,9,10,11],R2:[19,22,23,24,35,36,37]},\n \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\n \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":rationale,\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":counterevidence,\n \\\"limitations\\\":limitations,\n \\\"joint_history\\\":\\\"Two successive invocations of the same harness lineage, read separately and not combined: receipt 8b314551f1e049fcbf73a358f8ddf2c8 ran the fixed experiment 27bf7fc0875c4342966bd3dc15df80ec-experiment (resync and control cases) and receipt 9125b6a531234e7d9d2fa8cbb817df63 ran its declared successor 3ed5ddd94bce4e94a2dc5b7bb417c18a-experiment (same prefix and cases plus a single-follower case and a read of index 6). Both were produced from the same three-node setup (MemoryStorage, NoSnapshot entries, batch size 1, FIFO delivery without loss) with the same public endpoints; the successor reproduces the resync witness (events 22, 23, 24) and adds the isolated single-replica witness (event 35) and the leader-side hold (event 37). Event index 19 in both receipts is the same pre-resynchronization sampling point.\\\",\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\\\"entry_id\\\":K1,\\\"revision\\\":2,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"sync_log double-counts the StopSign when the resumed prefix already contains it\\\"},{\\\"entry_id\\\":K2,\\\"revision\\\":2,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"a re-synchronized replica's decided log read loses the entries\\\"},{\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"@inflation_applicability\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"the condition is the resume point covering the StopSign's index\\\"},{\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"@leader_decides_without_log_bound\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"the leader decides the reported accepted index without bounding it to its own log\\\"}]\n}\ngap={\\\"investigation_id\\\":QC,\n \\\"question\\\":\\\"Does the same inflation occur when T::Snapshot::use_snapshots() is true (the snapshot branch is not entered in the observed scenario because the sender's decided index equals the resume point), and can a leader's own accepted index be inflated when handle_majority_promises applies a follower's LogSync whose stopsign is Some and whose sync_idx already covers the StopSign?\\\"}\nquestion={\\\"id\\\":QC,\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"active\\\",\n \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"Whether a snapshot-enabled configuration reproduces the inflation or the sourced branch difference prevents it, and whether a new leader that already decided the StopSign is inflated when it syncs from a follower at a higher accepted round (the candidate's own decided index becomes sync_idx).\\\"}\n\nupdate={\\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Interpret the successor receipt, correct the knowledge it changes and register the remaining applicability question. The isolating run confirmed the follower-local consequence with a single re-synchronized replica (its endpoint flips and its decided-log read loses all six elements, receipt 9125b6a531234e7d9d2fa8cbb817df63 event 35) while the leader stayed consistent (event 37), which shows the leader's decision at the phantom index 7 requires a write quorum of inflated reports, as reproduced in events 22-24 of the same receipt and in the earlier receipt. The interpretation now covers both receipts with the same-run controls, a limitation narrows the consequence to index accounting and readability because the sealed configuration admits no further entries, the index-shift behavior is generalized to both observed decided-index positions, two behaviors/facts are added (the decision rule that ignores the leader's own log bound, and the sourced applicability condition including its independence from the snapshot option), and one gap is registered for the snapshot branch and for a new leader applying a follower's LogSync.\\\"),\n \\\"sources\\\":sources,\n \\\"investigations\\\":[question],\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[k2,k3,k4],\n \\\"gaps\\\":[gap],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[interp]}\njson.dump(update, open('update.json','w'), indent=1)\nprint('written')\nPY\ntimeout 120 /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_09-22-17-omnipaxos-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -c 2000\"","aggregated_output":"written\n{\"valid\": true, \"run_id\": \"d99e3b9fb63f4d89b4e0c59b4352dd5b\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 1002.1803323380009, \"diagnostics\": [], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\", \"no_change\": false, \"execution_requested\": false, \"effects\": [{\"object\": \"sources\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"create_diff_snapshot\"}, {\"object\": \"sources\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"no_stopsign_decided_idx\"}, {\"object\": \"knowledge\", \"action\": \"update\", \"target\": \"3ed5ddd94bce4e94a2dc5b7bb417c18a-knowledge-1\", \"changed_fields\": [\"statement\", \"conditions\", \"executions\"]}, {\"object\": \"knowledge\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"@inflation_applicability\"}, {\"object\": \"knowledge\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"@leader_decides_without_log_bound\"}, {\"object\": \"investigations\", \"action\": \"update\", \"target\": \"27bf7fc0875c4342966bd3dc15df80ec-question-0\", \"changed_fields\": [\"discriminator\", \"gaps\"]}, {\"object\": \"interpretations\", \"action\": \"append\", \"target\": \"interpretations[0]\", \"investigation_id\": \"27bf7fc0875c4342966bd3dc15df80ec-question-0\", \"changed_fields\": [\"experiment_id\", \"source_ids\", \"executions\", \"rationale\", \"answers\", \"knowledge\", \"counterevidence\", \"limitations\", \"joint_history\"]}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Interpreted the successor receipt and corrected the account. Receipt 9125b6a531234e7d9d2fa8cbb817df63 (same harness lineage with a third case added; all three tests passed) reproduced the re-synchronization witness (leader decided 7 with accepted 6, reconfiguration endpoint false, decided log unreadable: events 22, 23, 24) and isolated its two consequences: with only node 1 re-synchronized, node 1 alone ended at accepted 7 over the same six indices of content with decided 6, so its own reconfiguration endpoint flipped from true to false, its read of the StopSign's index 5 returned None while index 6 returned the StopSign, and its decided-log read from 0 returned an empty list where it had returned six elements (event 35); nodes 2 and 3 stayed at 6/6 with a six-element read and is_reconfigured true (events 36, 37), so the leader's decision at index 7 requires a write quorum of inflated reports. Declared comparisons matched: single-case comparisons 3-6 violated at index 35, leader-side comparisons 7-8 hold at index 37, and the baseline that index 6 held no StopSign before the re-synchronization holds at index 19. Updated records: the interpretation now covers both receipts (violated/asserted) with joint_history stating the two runs are read separately and not combined, counterevidence and limitations including the narrowing that the sealed configuration admits no further entries so no value is mis-assigned; the index-shift behavior was generalized to both observed decided-index positions and the decided-log read effect (one element with a quorum, empty list with a single report); a behavior was added for the leader deciding the reported accepted index without bounding it to its own log, and a sourced fact for the inflation's applicability condition (the resume point covering the StopSign's index, independent of the snapshot option because the snapshot branch derives sync_idx from get_decided_idx_without_stopsign); one gap was registered for the snapshot-enabled branch and for a new leader applying a follower's LogSync. Incomplete: that gap's execution, no snapshot-enabled run yet, the internal accepted-index vector behind the leader's phantom decision, and any independent second defect lead.\"}"}}
